# Fork distribution credits

T3 Code and the Arch packaging template come from the MIT-licensed
[upstream source](https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/tree/9cc4018c75ff4c61be8e86a6391d49a6c2d79830).
The distribution retains its [copyright and license](LICENSE).
The fork generates its local PKGBUILD from `packaging/aur/t3code-bin/PKGBUILD`
and preserves the maintainer credit and packaging functions.

The first-party Rust frame encoder, GNOME screen host and resource monitor
use the repository MIT license. Linux packages carry the license texts for
the selected Cargo dependencies beside their executables. The build resolves
the target graph from `native/desktop-native/Cargo.lock` and
`native/resource-monitor/Cargo.lock`. The frame notice includes the WebP
copyright, BSD license and patent grant supplied with libwebp-sys2 0.2.0.

The JavaScript and mobile distributions generate their notices from the
workspace lockfile and `third-party-licenses.config.json`.

