## Native Markdown parser and highlighting

Source: [enriched-markdown native sources](https://github.com/pingdotgg/enriched-markdown/tree/3757a4493bfce5be27fc90470ee3704bd903deec)
License: MIT for MD4C, tree-sitter and its grammars; the runtime's Unicode/ICU notice is retained separately in the linked notice resource.

- `apps/mobile/deps/react-native-enriched-markdown-1.2.0-t3.19-3757a449.tgz` (the four `cpp/enrmrkd/enrmrkd{,-entity}.{c,h}` files and `cpp/highlight/vendor/{generated,guarded}/generated_queries.h`): adapted; the fork retains MD4C parser sources and generates queries from the pinned tree-sitter grammars.
- `third-party/notices/enriched-markdown-native-3757a449.md`: copied notices with provenance headings; contains the exact MD4C header, runtime MIT license, complete Unicode/ICU notice, and all 19 grammar IDs' notices from 18 verified pinned npm archives. The resource distinguishes the fourteen default grammar IDs from the five optional ones and records each immutable artifact source and hash.

The mobile notice bundle includes this resource for the parser and native
highlighting sources. The pinned native runtime and grammar sources are
restored by the dependency's existing postinstall; no dependency is changed
by this attribution record.

